normal / OPLL — levels, canal compromise]\nPARAVERTEBRAL SOFT TISSUES: [normal]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Multilevel cervical spondylosis / No significant degenerative change].\n2. [Most significant level — disc protrusion type, cord contact/compression, myelopathic signal].\n3. [Foraminal stenosis — level, side, grade].\n4. [Myelopathy: T2 cord signal at [level] — correlate clinically].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
