","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Facets, Posterior Elements, and Sacrum","placeholder":"FACET JOINTS: [normal bilaterally / osteoarthropathy — levels, grade; synovial cysts — level, side, size, canal compromise]\nLIGAMENTUM FLAVUM: [normal / hypertrophy — levels, degree of canal compromise]\nSACROILIAC JOINTS: [normal / describe]\nPARAVERTEBRAL MUSCLES: [normal / fatty infiltration — grade]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Multilevel lumbar spondylosis / Focal pathology at specific level].\n2. [Most significant finding — disc herniation type, level, side, nerve root effect].\n3. [Canal stenosis — level, severity].\n4. [Foraminal stenosis — level, side, severity].\n5. [Spondylolisthesis / Spondylolysis — if present].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
