 'MRI Brain',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"MRCP was performed using heavily T2-weighted sequences (single-shot FSE and 3D MRCP) following fasting for 4 hours. Supplementary T1W in-phase/out-of-phase and T2W sequences of the liver and pancreas were obtained.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Obstructive jaundice / bile duct stones / PSC / recurrent pancreatitis / pancreatic cyst evaluation...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Biliary System","placeholder":"INTRAHEPATIC BILE DUCTS: [normal calibre throughout / dilatation — right > left / left > right / generalised; distribution: peripheral / central; most dilated duct: X mm]\nCOMMON HEPATIC DUCT: [calibre X mm — normal <7 mm]\nCOMMON BILE DUCT: [calibre X mm — normal <6 mm, post-cholecystectomy <10 mm]\nCALIBRE CHANGE / STRICTURE: [absent / present — location, length, abrupt/tapering]\nFILLING DEFECT: [absent / present — location, size, morphology: dependent (stone) / non-dependent (polyp/mass)]\nGALLBLADDER: [present/removed; stones/sludge; wall thickness; polyps]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Pancreatic Duct (Wirsung) and Parenchyma","placeholder":"MAIN PANCREATIC DUCT: [calibre — normal <3 mm: [X] mm throughout / focal dilatation at [location] — upstream obstruction]\nSIDEBRANCH DILATATION: [absent / present — location, size: X mm]\nPANCREATIC PARENCHYMA: [normal T1 signal and morphology / atrophy — head/body/tail; signal loss upstream of stricture]\nPERI-AMPULLARY REGION: [normal / filling defect / mass]\nANNULAR PANCREAS / PANCREAS DIVISUM: [absent / present]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Liver and Other","placeholder":"LIVER: [normal morphology and signal / focal lesion — describe; no significant hepatic steatosis]\nSPLEEN: [normal]\nPORTAL VEIN: [patent / thrombosis]\nLYMPH NODES: [no significant lymphadenopathy / enlarged — porta hepatis / coeliac]\nFREE FLUID: [absent / present]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Normal MRCP / Common bile duct calculus at [location], size [X] mm, proximal biliary dilatation to [X] mm].\n2. [Pancreatic duct — normal / dilated — cause].\n3. [Focal lesion — cyst type, IPMN branch/main duct, size, high-risk features].\n4. Recommendations: [ERCP / EUS / surgical review / follow-up MRCP in X months].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, false, 0),

