('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'X-Ray Chest - Normal',
 'Standard normal chest X-ray report with full systematic review',
 'X-Ray Chest',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"PA and lateral views of the chest.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Reason for examination...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings","placeholder":"LUNG FIELDS: The lungs are clear bilaterally. No focal consolidation, ground-glass opacity, or interstitial pattern. No pleural effusion or pneumothorax.\n\nHILA: The hilar shadows are of normal size and configuration bilaterally. No hilar lymphadenopathy.\n\nCARDIAC SILHOUETTE: The cardiac silhouette is not enlarged (cardiothoracic ratio within normal limits). The cardiac contours are normal.\n\nMEDIASTINUM: The mediastinal contour is unremarkable. The trachea is central. No mediastinal widening or mass.\n\nDIAPHRAGM AND COSTOPHRENIC ANGLES: Both hemidiaphragms are of normal position. The costophrenic angles are sharp bilaterally. No subphrenic free gas.\n\nOSSEOUS STRUCTURES: The ribs, clavicles, and visible thoracic spine are intact without acute fracture, metastatic lesion, or destructive change. Shoulder girdles are within normal limits.\n\nSOFT TISSUES: No subcutaneous emphysema. No soft tissue abnormality.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. No acute cardiopulmonary abnormality.","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, true, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'X-Ray Chest - Pneumonia / Consolidation',
