 'X-Ray Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Erect and supine views of the abdomen [and erect chest].","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Abdominal pain / distension / vomiting / suspected bowel obstruction / post-operative ileus...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings","placeholder":"GAS PATTERN:\n  SMALL BOWEL: [normal calibre / dilated — diameter >3 cm, number of loops, valvulae conniventes (complete loops), distribution]\n  LARGE BOWEL: [normal / dilated — diameter >6 cm, caecum >9 cm; haustra present/absent; transition point if visible]\n  GAS IN RECTUM: [present / absent]\n\nFREE INTRAPERITONEAL AIR: [absent / present — pneumoperitoneum; visible under right hemidiaphragm / Rigler sign / falciform ligament sign]\n\nSOFT TISSUE MASSES: [absent / describe — psoas shadows visible/obscured bilaterally]\n\nCALCIFICATIONS: [absent / renal calculi — side and position / gallstones / vascular calcification / pancreatic calcification / appendicolith]\n\nOSSEOUS STRUCTURES: [lower ribs, lumbar spine, pelvis — normal / describe]\n\nVISIBLE LUNG BASES: [clear / consolidation / effusion]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [No radiological evidence of bowel obstruction or free intraperitoneal air / Small bowel obstruction — dilated loops to X cm, no gas in colon/rectum / Large bowel obstruction — describe].\n2. [Free air — pneumoperitoneum].\n3. [Calcification — renal calculus right side / gallstones].\n4. [Recommendation: CT abdomen/pelvis for further assessment if clinically suspected].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
