 'Standard normal abdominal ultrasound with full organ assessment',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Ultrasound of the abdomen was performed with the patient in the supine and left lateral decubitus positions. Transverse and longitudinal views obtained with Doppler assessment of portal and hepatic vasculature.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Reason for examination...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings - Liver","placeholder":"The liver is normal in size with a smooth surface contour. Parenchymal echotexture is homogeneous. No focal hepatic lesion. No intrahepatic biliary dilatation. The portal vein is patent with normal hepatopetal flow on Doppler. The hepatic veins are patent.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Findings - Gallbladder and Biliary Tree","placeholder":"The gallbladder is normal in size with a wall thickness within normal limits. No gallstones, sludge, or polyps. No pericholecystic fluid. No sonographic Murphy sign. The common bile duct measures within normal limits (< 6 mm).","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Findings - Pancreas","placeholder":"The pancreas is normal in echotexture and calibre. The visible main pancreatic duct is not dilated. No focal pancreatic lesion. Peripancreatic fat is unremarkable.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Findings - Spleen","placeholder":"The spleen is normal in size, measuring [X] cm in long axis. Echotexture is homogeneous. No focal splenic lesion.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Findings - Kidneys","placeholder":"RIGHT KIDNEY: Measures [X] x [X] cm. Normal cortical thickness and echogenicity. Corticomedullary differentiation is maintained. No hydronephrosis, calculus, or focal mass.\nLEFT KIDNEY: Measures [X] x [X] cm. Normal cortical thickness and echogenicity. No hydronephrosis, calculus, or focal mass.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s8","label":"Findings - Aorta and Other","placeholder":"The abdominal aorta is normal in calibre, measuring [X] cm. No free intraperitoneal fluid. No para-aortic lymphadenopathy. The IVC is normal.","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s9","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. Normal abdominal ultrasound.\n2. No solid organ abnormality, biliary pathology, or hydronephrosis.","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, true, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen - Kidney Stone / Hydronephrosis',
 'Renal ultrasound for nephrolithiasis with hydronephrosis grading',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Ultrasound of the abdomen with focus on the urinary tract using greyscale and colour Doppler.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Flank pain / haematuria / suspected nephrolithiasis / urinary obstruction...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings - Right Kidney","placeholder":"Size: [X] x [X] cm\nCortical thickness and echogenicity: [normal / increased / decreased]\nCorticomedullary differentiation: [maintained / reduced]\nCalculus: [absent / present — location: upper/mid/lower pole / renal pelvis; size: [X] mm; echogenic focus with posterior acoustic shadowing: [present]]\nHydronephrosis: [absent / grade 1 mild — pelvic dilatation only / grade 2 moderate — calyces dilated / grade 3 severe — parenchymal thinning]\nPerinephric collection: [absent / present]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Findings - Left Kidney","placeholder":"Size: [X] x [X] cm\nCortical thickness and echogenicity: [normal]\nCalculus: [absent / present — location, size]\nHydronephrosis: [absent / grade — as above]\nPerinephric collection: [absent]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Findings - Bladder","placeholder":"Urinary bladder: [adequately/poorly distended]\nWall thickness: [normal ≤3 mm when distended]\nIntraluminal contents: [anechoic urine / echogenic debris / calculus — size, posterior shadow]\nUreteric jets: [present bilaterally / absent right/left — suggesting obstruction]\nPre/post-void residual (if obtained): [X] ml","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Findings - Other Abdomen","placeholder":"Liver: [normal]\nGallbladder: [normal / stones]\nPancreas: [normal / obscured by bowel gas]\nSpleen: [normal]\nAorta: [normal calibre]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Right/Left/Bilateral] renal calculus, measuring [X] mm, [upper/mid/lower pole / renal pelvis].\n2. [Mild/Moderate/Severe / No] hydronephrosis on the [right/left].\n3. [Ureteric calculus if visible — location, size].\n4. Contralateral kidney: [normal].\n5. [Ureteric jets present/absent — Doppler findings].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[{"id":"c1","trigger_keyword":"kidney stone","add_section":"Findings - Right Kidney","section_content":"Renal calculus: location (pole), size (mm), echogenic focus with posterior acoustic shadowing, associated hydronephrosis grade, perinephric changes."},{"id":"c2","trigger_keyword":"hydronephrosis","add_section":"Findings - Right Kidney","section_content":"Hydronephrosis grading: Grade 1 (pelvis only), Grade 2 (pelvis + calyces), Grade 3 (severe — parenchymal thinning). Assess ureteric jets with colour Doppler."}]'::jsonb,
 false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen - Gallstones / Cholecystitis',
 'Gallbladder ultrasound with cholecystitis assessment and sonographic Murphy sign',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Ultrasound of the upper abdomen with focus on the gallbladder and biliary tree, performed after 6 hours fasting. Greyscale and colour Doppler.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Right upper quadrant pain / suspected cholecystitis / jaundice...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings - Gallbladder","placeholder":"Gallbladder dimensions: [X] x [X] cm (long axis x width)\nWall thickness: [X] mm (normal ≤3 mm)\nGallstones: [absent / single / multiple — size of largest: [X] mm; posterior acoustic shadowing: present; mobile: yes/no]\nSludge: [absent / present]\nPolyps: [absent / present — size [X] mm, number]\nPericholecystic fluid: [absent / present — trace / significant]\nSonographic Murphy sign: [positive / negative / equivocal]\nGallbladder distension (hydrops): [absent / present — wall-echo-shadow (WES) sign]\nIntramural gas: [absent / present — emphysematous cholecystitis]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Findings - Biliary Tree","placeholder":"COMMON BILE DUCT (CBD): [calibre X mm — normal ≤6 mm; post-cholecystectomy ≤10 mm]\nINTRAHEPATIC BILE DUCTS: [not dilated / dilated — distribution: central/peripheral; degree: mild/moderate/severe]\nBILIARY STONE: [absent / CBD stone — size, location]\nPNEUMOBILIA: [absent / present]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Findings - Liver and Other","placeholder":"LIVER: [normal echotexture and size / steatosis — mild/moderate/severe / focal lesion]\nPANCREAS: [normal / head enlargement]\nPORTAL VEIN: [patent, hepatopetal flow]\nFREE FLUID: [absent / present — perisplenic / pericholecystic / generalised ascites]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Cholelithiasis — multiple gallstones, largest [X] mm / No gallstones].\n2. [Acute cholecystitis — gallbladder wall thickening [X] mm, positive sonographic Murphy sign, pericholecystic fluid / No features of acute cholecystitis].\n3. [CBD stones / dilated CBD — [X] mm — ?cause]\n4. Recommendation: [urgent surgical review / MRCP / ERCP / hepatobiliary surgery].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[{"id":"c1","trigger_keyword":"cholecystitis","add_section":"Findings - Gallbladder","section_content":"Features of acute cholecystitis: wall thickening >3 mm, positive sonographic Murphy sign, pericholecystic fluid, gallstones. Assess for emphysematous cholecystitis (intramural gas)."}]'::jsonb,
 false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Pelvis - Normal (Female)',
 'Standard female pelvic ultrasound with endometrial measurement and adnexal assessment',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Transabdominal pelvic ultrasound performed with a full urinary bladder, followed by transvaginal ultrasound (if consented and clinically indicated).","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Pelvic pain / irregular bleeding / adnexal mass / fertility assessment...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Findings - Uterus","placeholder":"POSITION: [anteverted / retroverted / axial]\nSIZE: [X] x [X] x [X] cm (length x AP x width)\nMYOMETRIUM: [normal homogeneous echotexture / fibroid — location: submucosal/intramural/subserosal; size: [X] mm; number]\nENDOMETRIUM: [thickness: [X] mm; morphology: regular/irregular; echogenicity: normal/hyperechoic/heterogeneous]\nCERVIX: [normal]\nFIBROIDS: [absent / present — describe as above]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Findings - Right Ovary","placeholder":"Size: [X] x [X] x [X] cm\nEchotexture: [normal homogeneous with follicles]\nDominant follicle: [present — [X] mm / absent]\nSimple cyst: [absent / present — size [X] mm]\nComplex cyst: [absent / present — morphology: solid component/septations/Doppler]\nOverall: [normal / describe abnormality]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Findings - Left Ovary","placeholder":"Size: [X] x [X] x [X] cm\nEchotexture: [normal homogeneous with follicles]\nSimple cyst: [absent / present — size [X] mm]\nComplex cyst: [absent / present]\nOverall: [normal / describe abnormality]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Findings - Other","placeholder":"POUCH OF DOUGLAS (cul-de-sac): [no free fluid / trace free fluid — anechoic, physiological / complex fluid — describe]\nBLADDER: [normal wall thickness; no intraluminal mass]\nPERITONEUM: [no evidence of peritoneal deposits]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Normal pelvic ultrasound / Uterine fibroid(s) — describe].\n2. [Normal ovaries / Right/left ovarian cyst — simple/complex, size — IOTA criteria assessment].\n3. [No free fluid / Trace free fluid — physiological].\n4. Recommendation: [follow-up ultrasound in X weeks / MRI pelvis / gynaecology review].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, true, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Thyroid - Nodule / Assessment',
 'Thyroid ultrasound with TI-RADS classification for nodules',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"High-resolution ultrasound of the thyroid gland with 7–15 MHz linear transducer, supplemented with colour Doppler. Both lobes and isthmus imaged in transverse and longitudinal planes.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Thyroid nodule / goitre / thyrotoxicosis / neck mass / post-thyroidectomy follow-up...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Thyroid Gland - Overall","placeholder":"RIGHT LOBE: [X] x [X] x [X] cm (AP x transverse x length)\nLEFT LOBE: [X] x [X] x [X] cm\nISTHMUS: [X] mm (AP)\nGLAND VOLUME (if calculated): [X] mL (normal female <18 mL, male <25 mL)\nECHOTEXTURE: [normal homogeneous / heterogeneous — diffuse / focal changes]\nDOPPLER: [normal flow pattern / increased vascularity — diffuse (Graves) / focal]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Nodule Assessment (list each nodule)","placeholder":"NODULE 1:\n  Lobe: [right/left], Location: [upper/mid/lower pole]\n  Size: [X] x [X] x [X] mm\n  Composition: [solid / predominantly solid / predominantly cystic / cystic / spongiform]\n  Echogenicity: [hyperechoic / isoechoic / hypoechoic / markedly hypoechoic]\n  Shape: [wider-than-tall / taller-than-wide]\n  Margins: [smooth / ill-defined / lobulated / irregular / extra-thyroidal extension]\n  Echogenic foci: [none / macrocalcification / peripheral calcification (eggshell) / punctate echogenic foci (PEF — suspicious) / comet tail artefact]\n  ACR TI-RADS: Category [1/2/3/4/5] — [benign / not suspicious / mildly suspicious / moderately suspicious / highly suspicious]\n  Recommendation: [no FNA / FNA if ≥X cm / follow-up at X months]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Cervical Lymph Nodes","placeholder":"CERVICAL LYMPH NODES (levels II–VI bilaterally): [no sonographically suspicious lymph nodes / suspicious node at — level, side, size, morphology: round, loss of hilum, microcalcification, cystic change]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Normal thyroid / Multinodular goitre / Diffuse heterogeneous thyroid — consistent with thyroiditis].\n2. Nodule(s): [describe dominant nodule — ACR TI-RADS X, size X mm, [right/left] lobe — FNA recommended/not recommended based on size threshold].\n3. [No suspicious cervical lymphadenopathy].\n4. Recommendation: [follow ACR TI-RADS management guidelines / ultrasound follow-up in X months / FNA biopsy].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, true, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Obstetric - First Trimester',
 'First trimester obstetric ultrasound with GA, viability, and NT measurement',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"First trimester ultrasound performed transabdominally and transvaginally (as required) for optimal visualisation of the uterine contents.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Pregnancy dating / viability assessment / bleeding in pregnancy / nuchal translucency screening...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Gestational Sac","placeholder":"LOCATION: [intrauterine — fundal/mid/lower uterine segment / extra-uterine — specify]\nMEAN SAC DIAMETER (MSD): [X] mm\nGESTATIONAL AGE BY MSD: [X] weeks [X] days\nYOLK SAC: [present — normal morphology / absent / abnormal — describe]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Fetal Assessment","placeholder":"NUMBER OF FETUSES: [singleton / twins — dichorionic-diamniotic / monochorionic-diamniotic / monochorionic-monoamniotic]\nCROWN-RUMP LENGTH (CRL): [X] mm\nGESTATIONAL AGE BY CRL: [X] weeks [X] days (range ±7 days)\nFETAL CARDIAC ACTIVITY: [present — rate [X] bpm (normal 100–170 bpm at 6–10 weeks) / absent]\nFETAL MOVEMENTS: [present / absent]\nNUCHAL TRANSLUCENCY (if 11–13+6 weeks): [X] mm (normal <3.5 mm; MoM: [X])","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Uterus and Adnexa","placeholder":"UTERINE FIBROIDS: [absent / present — location, size]\nRETROPLACENTAL COLLECTION: [absent / present]\nSUBCHORIONIC HAEMATOMA: [absent / present — size: [X] x [X] mm; location]\nADNEXA: [right: normal / corpus luteum — size [X] mm / describe. Left: normal / describe]\nFREE FLUID: [absent / present — amount]","required":false,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Estimated GA and EDD","placeholder":"BY CRL: [X] weeks [X] days\nBY LMP (if provided): [X] weeks [X] days (LMP: [date])\nEDD (by CRL): [date]\nCORRELATION: [dates concordant / discrepancy of [X] days — use CRL dating if >7 days discrepancy]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s7","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Intrauterine / Extra-uterine] singleton pregnancy.\n2. Viability: [viable — fetal cardiac activity present at [X] bpm].\n3. Estimated gestational age by CRL: [X] weeks [X] days. EDD: [date].\n4. Nuchal translucency: [X] mm — [within normal limits / increased — refer for further assessment].\n5. [Subchorionic haematoma / Adnexal finding / Other].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Scrotal - Testicular Assessment',
 'Scrotal ultrasound for testicular pathology, epididymitis, and torsion',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"High-resolution scrotal ultrasound performed with a 7–15 MHz linear transducer. Greyscale and colour/spectral Doppler interrogation of both testes and epididymes.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Scrotal pain / scrotal mass / infertility / trauma / suspected torsion / varicocele...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Right Testis and Epididymis","placeholder":"RIGHT TESTIS:\n  Size: [X] x [X] x [X] mm\n  Volume: [X] mL (normal 15–25 mL)\n  Echotexture: [homogeneous / heterogeneous — describe]\n  Focal lesion: [absent / present — size, location, echotexture, posterior enhancement, calcification]\n  Vascular flow (colour Doppler): [normal / increased / absent — symmetry with contralateral]\n  Mediastinum testis: [normal]\n\nRIGHT EPIDIDYMIS:\n  Head: [normal — [X] mm / enlarged/heterogeneous — describe]\n  Body/Tail: [normal / thickened]\n  Epididymo-orchitis: [absent / present]\n  Vascular flow: [normal / increased]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Left Testis and Epididymis","placeholder":"LEFT TESTIS:\n  Size: [X] x [X] x [X] mm\n  Volume: [X] mL\n  Echotexture: [homogeneous / heterogeneous]\n  Focal lesion: [absent / present]\n  Vascular flow: [normal / increased / absent]\n\nLEFT EPIDIDYMIS:\n  Head: [normal]\n  Body/Tail: [normal]\n  Vascular flow: [normal]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Scrotal Contents and Other","placeholder":"HYDROCELE: [absent / right / left / bilateral — simple anechoic / complex; size: small/moderate/large]\nVARICOCELE: [absent / left / bilateral — calibre >3 mm; augmentation with Valsalva: present/absent; grade I/II/III]\nSPERMATOCELE/EPIDIDYMAL CYST: [absent / present — side, location, size]\nSCROTAL WALL: [normal / thickened / oedema]\nTORSION ASSESSMENT: [if clinically relevant — rotation, absence of flow, heterogeneity, reactive hydrocele]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Normal testicular echotexture and vascularity bilaterally / Focal testicular lesion — right/left, size, characteristics — urgent urology referral].\n2. [Epididymo-orchitis — right/left].\n3. [Varicocele — left/bilateral, grade X].\n4. [Hydrocele — right/left/bilateral].\n5. [Torsion — absent Doppler flow right/left — URGENT surgical exploration].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[{"id":"c1","trigger_keyword":"torsion","add_section":"Right Testis and Epididymis","section_content":"Testicular torsion protocol: assess for absent/reduced Doppler flow, heterogeneous echotexture, enlarged epididymis, reactive hydrocele. If absent flow — URGENT surgical exploration. Do not delay for additional imaging."},{"id":"c2","trigger_keyword":"testicular mass","add_section":"Right Testis and Epididymis","section_content":"Focal testicular lesion: size, location, echotexture (hypo/hyperechoic/heterogeneous), posterior features, calcification, Doppler vascularity. Urgent urology referral for all solid intratesticular lesions."}]'::jsonb,
 false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Carotid Doppler - Stenosis Assessment',
 'Carotid duplex ultrasound with NASCET stenosis grading and plaque characterisation',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Bilateral carotid duplex ultrasound performed using a 7–12 MHz linear transducer with greyscale, colour Doppler, and spectral waveform analysis of the common carotid arteries (CCAs), carotid bifurcations, internal carotid arteries (ICAs), external carotid arteries (ECAs), and vertebral arteries.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"TIA / stroke / carotid bruit / atherosclerosis screening / pre-operative assessment...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Right Carotid","placeholder":"RIGHT CCA:\n  Calibre: [normal]\n  IMT (intima-media thickness): [X] mm (normal <0.9 mm)\n  Plaque: [absent / present — location: bifurcation/distal CCA; morphology: echogenic/echolucent/heterogeneous/calcified; surface: smooth/ulcerated/irregular]\n\nRIGHT ICA (BIFURCATION / PROXIMAL):\n  Stenosis: [absent / present — NASCET grade: <50% mild / 50–69% moderate / 70–99% severe / occlusion]\n  Peak systolic velocity (PSV): [X] cm/s (threshold for >70%: >230 cm/s)\n  End-diastolic velocity (EDV): [X] cm/s\n  ICA/CCA ratio: [X] (ratio >4 = >70%)\n  Waveform: [normal / monophasic / dampened]\n\nRIGHT ECA: [patent / stenosis]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Left Carotid","placeholder":"LEFT CCA:\n  IMT: [X] mm\n  Plaque: [absent / present — describe as above]\n\nLEFT ICA:\n  Stenosis: [absent / present — NASCET grade]\n  PSV: [X] cm/s\n  EDV: [X] cm/s\n  ICA/CCA ratio: [X]\n  Waveform: [normal / dampened]\n\nLEFT ECA: [patent / stenosis]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Vertebral Arteries","placeholder":"RIGHT VERTEBRAL ARTERY: [patent, antegrade flow / absent / hypoplastic / reversed flow — subclavian steal]\nLEFT VERTEBRAL ARTERY: [patent, antegrade flow / absent / reversed flow — subclavian steal]\nDominance: [right / left / co-dominant / hypoplastic right/left]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [No significant carotid stenosis bilaterally / Right ICA: [NASCET grade] stenosis — [mild/moderate/severe] / Left ICA: [NASCET grade] stenosis]\n2. [Atherosclerotic plaque — bilateral carotid bifurcations, morphology]\n3. [IMT: [X] mm bilaterally — [normal / increased]]\n4. [Vertebral arteries: [normal / reversed flow — subclavian steal]]\n5. Recommendation: [neurosurgical/vascular review for ≥70% stenosis / repeat Doppler in X months / CT angiography for confirmation / stenting/endarterectomy consideration].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound DVT Lower Limb - Compression',
 'Lower limb venous duplex ultrasound for deep vein thrombosis',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"Lower limb venous duplex ultrasound of the [right/left/bilateral] lower extremity performed with greyscale and colour Doppler. Compression ultrasound applied at 2 cm intervals from inguinal ligament to popliteal fossa, including calf veins if symptomatic.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Leg swelling / pain / suspected DVT / Wells score [X] — [low/intermediate/high] pre-test probability. D-dimer: [value / not performed].","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Right Lower Limb Venous Assessment","placeholder":"COMMON FEMORAL VEIN (CFV): [fully compressible — no thrombus / non-compressible — thrombus: acute/chronic; extent: partial/occlusive]\nSAPHENOFEMORAL JUNCTION: [normal / involved]\nFEMORAL VEIN (FV proximal and mid): [compressible / non-compressible]\nDEEP FEMORAL VEIN: [compressible / not assessed]\nPOPLITEAL VEIN: [compressible / non-compressible]\nCALF VEINS (if assessed): [peroneal / posterior tibial / gastrocnemial / soleal — compressible / non-compressible]\nBAKER CYST: [absent / present — ruptured / intact, size]\nDOPPLER WAVEFORM: [phasic with respiration / absent phasicity — proximal obstruction]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Left Lower Limb Venous Assessment","placeholder":"COMMON FEMORAL VEIN: [compressible / non-compressible]\nFEMORAL VEIN: [compressible / non-compressible]\nPOPLITEAL VEIN: [compressible / non-compressible]\nCALF VEINS: [compressible / non-compressible]\nDOPPLER WAVEFORM: [phasic / absent phasicity]\nFOCO FINDING: [none / incidental — Baker cyst / soft tissue mass]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [No evidence of deep vein thrombosis in the [right/left/bilateral] lower limb(s)] — [fully compressible venous system from inguinal ligament to popliteal fossa].\n[OR: Deep vein thrombosis identified in the [right/left] [proximal (iliofemoral/femoral/popliteal) / distal (calf)] venous system — [acute: hypoechoic, non-compressible, vessel expansion / chronic: echogenic, partially recanalized]].\n2. [Extent: from [vein] to [vein]].\n3. [Baker cyst — intact / ruptured — alternative cause of symptoms].\n4. Recommendation: [anticoagulation — haematology/vascular review / repeat US in 5–7 days if isolated calf DVT / urgent vascular if phlegmasia cerulea dolens].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[{"id":"c1","trigger_keyword":"DVT","add_section":"Right Lower Limb Venous Assessment","section_content":"DVT identified: non-compressible vein segment — characterise as acute (hypoechoic, vessel expansion) or chronic (echogenic, recanalized). Map full extent from CFV to calf. Assess contralateral limb."}]'::jsonb,
 false, 0),

('00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000',
 'Ultrasound Breast - Mass / Assessment',
 'Breast ultrasound with ACR BI-RADS US classification for mass characterisation',
 'Ultrasound Abdomen',
 '[{"id":"s1","label":"Technique","placeholder":"High-resolution ultrasound of the [right/left/bilateral] breast performed with a 10–15 MHz linear transducer in radial and anti-radial planes, supplemented by colour Doppler.","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s2","label":"Clinical Indication","placeholder":"Palpable lump / mammographic abnormality / nipple discharge / breast pain / axillary mass...","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s3","label":"Breast Parenchyma","placeholder":"BREAST COMPOSITION: [predominantly fatty / scattered fibroglandular / heterogeneous / extremely dense] — [approximately X% glandular]\nSKIN THICKNESS: [normal / thickened — [X] mm]\nNIPPLE AND SUBAREOLAR REGION: [normal / discharge / inversion / mass]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s4","label":"Mass / Lesion Characterisation (BI-RADS US)","placeholder":"LESION 1:\n  Location: [right/left breast, clock position: X o''clock, depth: anterior/middle/posterior third, distance from nipple: X cm]\n  Size: [X] x [X] x [X] mm\n  SHAPE: [oval / round / irregular]\n  ORIENTATION: [parallel (wider than tall) / not parallel (taller than wide) — more suspicious]\n  MARGIN: [circumscribed / not circumscribed: angular/microlobulated/indistinct/spiculated]\n  ECHO PATTERN: [anechoic / hyperechoic / complex cystic and solid / hypoechoic / isoechoic / heterogeneous]\n  POSTERIOR FEATURES: [no posterior features / enhancement / shadowing / combined]\n  CALCIFICATIONS: [absent / present — macro/micro]\n  DOPPLER: [avascular / peripheral / internal vascularity]\n  ACR BI-RADS: [0/1/2/3/4A/4B/4C/5]\n  Recommendation: [routine follow-up / short-term follow-up in 6 months / biopsy]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s5","label":"Axilla","placeholder":"AXILLARY LYMPH NODES (right): [normal — cortical thickness <3 mm, fatty hilum present / abnormal — cortical thickening >3 mm, loss of hilum, round morphology; size of largest: [X] mm]\nAXILLARY LYMPH NODES (left): [normal / abnormal — describe]","required":true,"type":"text"},{"id":"s6","label":"Impression","placeholder":"1. [Right/Left/Bilateral breast]: [No suspicious mass — BI-RADS 1/2 / Simple cyst — BI-RADS 2 / Probably benign oval circumscribed hypoechoic mass — BI-RADS 3 — short-term follow-up / Suspicious mass — BI-RADS 4A/4B/4C — biopsy recommended / Highly suspicious — BI-RADS 5 — biopsy mandatory].\n2. [Axillary lymphadenopathy — right/left — abnormal morphology].\n3. Recommendation: [management per BI-RADS guidelines — describe].","required":true,"type":"text"}]'::jsonb,
 '[]'::jsonb, false, 0),

